Ratan Tata. They will implement these lessons through relatable case studies., Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Sachin Tendulkar and Ratan Tata. They will implement these lessons through relatable case studies.; Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Active listening requires focused attention, interpretation, clarification and feedback. It supports understanding by checking meaning instead of assuming.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Active listening is an essential part of academic progress and communications. Students will learn to listen with their eyes; ears; mind; and heart.. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

